  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When shaders are blocked, VRChat has a list of fallback shaders they default to. VRC chooses the shader most similar / appropriate automatically.\n\nCurrently, the internal shaders just really don't cut it though. The vast majority of avatars look completely wrong if custom shaders aren't enabled.\n\nIt would be nice if most avatars look fine, even if custom shaders are disabled, that way we can block ANNOYING shaders without also essentially breaking the game's appearance completely.\n\nThus, I vote that the number of internal shaders should be expanded upon, so that the most popular safe shaders are a available even if custom shaders are blocked.\n\nTo start on a list of safe shaders:\n\nCubed's Unity Shaders: https://github.com/cubedparadox/Cubeds-Unity-Shaders\nSilent's Cel Shading Shaders (SCSS): https://vrcat.club/threads/silents-cel-shading-shader.84/\nNoeNoe's Shaders: https://vrcat.club/threads/updated-29-5-18-noenoe-shaders.157/\nPoiyomi's Toon Shaders\nArkToon Shaders: https://vrcat.club/threads/arktoon-shaders.2727/\nMochie's Uber Shader\nXiexe's Toon Shader: https://vrcat.club/threads/xiexes-toon-shader-v2-0-updated-3-11-2019-xstoon-the-rewrite.1878/\n\nI do believe this is most of the common safe shaders. Of course it's best you get in-touch with their creators to get an approval first, but I'm sure they'd be fine with it - proud of themselves even, perhaps.\n\nIf you'd like or think the community would appreciate it - You could add a feature to the shader blocking to have two levels of shader blocking - \"Moderate\" and \"Strict\". Moderate would block custom shaders outside of this whitelist, but still allow community-approved shaders like the ones I referred to, which would allow one to block troublesome shaders without making the whole game ugly. \"Strict\" would work like the current shader blocking does.\n\nJust a suggestion I figured I'd put out there. Thanks!",
